node_modules/
dist/
.env
.env.local
*.log
.DS_Store
.vite/
.vercel/

# Source-of-truth drops. These are the raw deliveries — the multi-hundred-MB
# sculpts and the un-optimised exports — and they stay out.
assets/*.glb
apps/kiosk/public/models/*.tflite

# Vision runtime: the wasm is copied out of node_modules and the models are
# downloaded, both by `npm run vision:assets`. Reproducible from the lockfile
# plus that script, so committing ~10MB of binaries buys nothing — the Vercel
# build runs the same script, which is why these can stay ignored and the cloud
# deploy still sees.
apps/kiosk/public/mediapipe/
apps/kiosk/public/models/*.task

# The raw delivery location for rendered answers stays ignored...
assets/fallback/*.mp3

# ...but the *served* copies are committed, deliberately.
#
# These two exceptions (the optimised GLB, ~1.3MB, and the answer bank, ~1.3MB)
# reverse the original out-of-band rule for the only two assets the app cannot
# degrade past. Without them a deploy is a placeholder cube that says nothing,
# which is not a reviewable kiosk. 2.6MB is not "large binary assets" — the rule
# was written against the 1.9M-tri sculpt, and it still holds for that.
#
# The cost is real and worth naming: the MP3s are dummy audio and will be
# re-rendered, and each re-render is another 1.3MB of history that never shrinks.
# If the bank gets re-rendered more than a couple of times, move it to Vercel
# Blob and delete these lines rather than letting the repo carry every take.
!apps/kiosk/public/models/enubot.glb
!apps/kiosk/public/fallback/*.mp3
